pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% DEFECT: `conclusion ENUMERATION_COMPLETE` accepted a contradiction manufactured
% by the objective-improving constraint of `soli`. That constraint (`obj <= v-1`)
% removes every assignment with objective value at least `v` and, unlike `solx`,
% never increments the excluded-solution counter, so the contradiction it creates
% does not establish "there are no further solutions". This formula has three
% solutions and two projections onto the preserved variable x1, so a complete
% enumeration of 0 solutions is wrong under every reading.
f 1;
soli ~x1 x2;
output NONE;
conclusion ENUMERATION_COMPLETE 0;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
